  "summary": "Performance-driven urban dress: taped seams, storm-proof shells, modular straps and a black-clad cyber-utility silhouette.",
  "description": "Techwear applies technical outdoor and military apparel engineering — Gore-Tex laminates, laser-cut vents, articulated patterns — to city wear, crystallized by ACRONYM (Errolson Hugh & Michaela Sachenbacher) from 1994/2002 and popularized through cyberpunk imagery, ninja-scientist silhouettes and brands like Acronym, Nike ACG collaborations and numerous house brands. It proposes clothes as exoskeleton: waterproof, modular, monochrome. Adjacent: gorpcore (casual outdoor-wear adoption).",
